# Testing

- Cover each important behavior with an automated test in the same change.
- Use PostgreSQL for tests that run SQL. Do not point those tests at SQLite.
- A test that cannot run must fail with an explicit error. Do not mark it skipped to hide a broken dependency.
- Report the command, the exit code, and the counts. Do not paraphrase a run that did not happen.
- Health, migration, credential, and bucket-privacy checks are part of Stage 1 and must keep passing.
